    <Description>
      <One_Line_Description_Summary>CalcExpress</One_Line_Description_Summary>
      <Description>CalcExpress Toolkit is a comprehensive suite of VIs and interactive tools used to execute text-based scripts and evaluate formulas natively within LabVIEW. It includes a script engine (CSE), a formula parser (CalcExpress), a centralized data management framework (VarMan), and several advanced utility VIs. It is compatible with &lt;b&gt;32-bit&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;64-bit&lt;/b&gt; LabVIEW for Windows.

Integrating scripts into your application allows for dynamic changes to the system's behavior at runtime without the need to modify or recompile the core LabVIEW source code. These scripts are not limited to mathematical calculations; they can be utilized for a broad variety of tasks such as instrument control, test sequence execution, data communication, and localized hardware data collection. Applications can also benefit from completely automated data logging when running scripts or using VarMan runtime variables.

&lt;b&gt;Key Features&lt;/b&gt;
*) The script syntax is highly intuitive, closely matching the conventions of the LabVIEW Formula Node and the C language. A script can feature loops, conditional branches, and jumps alongside standard expression evaluations.
*) Supported data types natively include numeric scalars (both real and complex numbers), strings, and arrays thereof. Custom, user-defined data types can also be integrated seamlessly.
*) Script operators and functions are fully polymorphic, behaving exactly like native LabVIEW primitives.
*) Over 250 predefined functions are available out-of-the-box to handle complex calculations, digital signal processing, array manipulation, file I/O operations, asynchronous VI control, synchronization, and user interaction.
*) User-defined functions can be easily implemented as standard VIs, referred to as FuncVIs. Utilizing the FuncVI mechanism, users can expand the CalcExpress vocabulary with custom functions of any complexity level.
*) The Variable Manager (VarMan) serves as an essential engine component, facilitating exclusive or cooperative thread-safe access to memory variables for application blocks and running scripts. Applications can dynamically create, destroy, and manipulate variables and their metadata properties on the fly.
*) VarMan supports automatic background historical tracking for active variables, providing a robust foundation for automated data logging across your system.
*) The CalcExpress execution core is fully reentrant and multithreaded, enabling it to independently execute multiple scripts simultaneously without performance bottlenecks.

### Function and Control Palettes
The CalcExpress function and control palettes can be found within the native LabVIEW Addons palette: &lt;b&gt;Addons &gt;&gt; CalcExpress&lt;/b&gt;. Menu configuration file: `&lt;LabVIEW&gt;\vi.lib\addons\CalcExpress\dir.mnu`

### Utilities and Examples
Integrated utilities can be launched from the main LabVIEW toolbar under the &lt;b&gt;Tools &gt;&gt; CalcExpress&lt;/b&gt; menu. Select the "Examples Navigator" from this menu to visually browse and run the packaged example VIs.

### Documentation
The complete CalcExpress help manual can be accessed at any time via the &lt;b&gt;Help &gt;&gt; CalcExpress&lt;/b&gt; menu. Additionally, you can open the user help file and supplementary reference materials using the &lt;b&gt;Tools &gt;&gt; CalcExpress &gt;&gt; Help and Support&lt;/b&gt; menu shortcut.
</Description>
      <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2000-2026, Konstantin Shifershteyn</Copyright>
      <Packager>Konstantin Shifershteyn</Packager>
      <URL>https://github.com/konstantin-shifershteyn/calcexpress</URL>
      <Release_Notes>
&lt;b&gt;VERSION 4.0.0&lt;/b&gt;
CalcExpress has transitioned to a fully Open-Source project under the MIT License. All LabVIEW VIs, C engine code, and core assets are now publicly accessible.

REPOSITORY:
https://github.com/konstantin-shifershteyn/calcexpress

KEY UPDATES &amp; NEW FEATURES
* Script Syntax is extended with Named Constants and inline Parsing Directives.
* Script Engine utilizes a new documented way of implicit conversion of DBL values to 32-bit integers.
* Script Engine VIs were updated and new VIs added.
* Predefined Script Functions were updated and new functions added.
* Variable Manager supports tracking Writer IDs and lifecycle update statistics.
* Variable Manager has got new variable control VIs and batch read/write VIs.
* VarMan Spy utility supports name filtering, metric tracking, resizable inspector windows, and automatic UI window property saving.
* CSE ISP utility supports right-click context-sensitive help for basic syntax elements.
* Engine Core DLL code has been revamped to add new features, improve performance, and fix known issues.
* Documentation has updated content. It eliminates insecure third-party JavaScript dependencies now.
* etc.

&lt;b&gt;VERSION 3.0.1&lt;/b&gt;
* Bug fixes and updates to the core code, user utilities, predefined functions, and documentation.

&lt;b&gt;VERSION 3.0.0&lt;/b&gt;
* CalcExpress Toolkit can be used with both &lt;b&gt;32-bit&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;64-bit&lt;/b&gt; LabVIEW.
* Core DLL code has been revamped to add new features, improve performance, and fix known issues.
* Revamped CalcExpress documentation is provided in the Compiled HTML Help format (.CHM file).
* Scripts syntax extended.
* VIs, utilities and examples updated.
* etc.
</Release_Notes>
    </Description>
